# Internship Finder Project Rules

## Product Definition
- Internship Finder is a domain-specific deep research agent, not a generic job board.

## Tech Stack & Execution
- UI & Session: Next.js (App Router) on Vercel.
- CSS: Vanilla CSS / CSS Modules (Strictly NO TailwindCSS, Mobile-First enforced).
- Database: Supabase (Auth, Postgres DB, Storage).
- Background Execution: GitHub Actions (or similar asynchronous worker) for all recursive research.
- AI: Google Gemini.

## Architectural Constraints
- Asynchronous Research: Web scraping, domain expansion, and iterative research MUST NOT run synchronously within Vercel HTTP requests.
- Pluggable Providers: The search architecture must support multiple swappable search/extraction providers.
- Feature-Based Structure: Organize code by domain under `src/features/`.

## AI & Resource Rules
- Deterministic First: Always use standard code (SQL, normalization, regex) before invoking an LLM.
- AI Limits: Use AI ONLY for profile analysis, adaptive enrichment, domain expansion, semantic matching, and explanation generation.
- Batching & Caching: Batch AI calls and cache reusable semantic outputs to protect API limits.

## Data Quality & Deduplication
- Canonical Identifiers: Deduplicate internships deterministically using `company + role + location`.
- Provenance: Retain all discovered source URLs for an internship. Always prefer official company career pages.
- Validation: Validate listing status deterministically before relying on AI.

## Onboarding
- Multi-path: Always offer multiple ways to onboard (Resume, LinkedIn URL, Quick Start).
- Confidence Score: Research cannot begin until the user's Profile Confidence Score reaches the required threshold, achieved via conversational AI enrichment if necessary.
